; Leg EJ -- EDIT 23 WITNESS.  The only leg that can see edit 23.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
;  VICTOR RUNS D:\CKFNFD.EXE -- the KEEP_DEBUG build, md5 64ba06ed... --
;  with --xonxoff.  CKFNF.EXE is NODEBUG and writes no log.
;
;  THE RESULT IS ONE LINE OF D:\DEBUG.LOG:
;      v9k_ser_setflow crtscts/ixon [0] 1
;  It has read 0 for this port's whole life.  Edit 23 must make it 1.
;
;  Small fixture on purpose: -d costs ~25 ms per received byte (SS16k),
;  so this leg's clock is meaningless and is not a result.
;  Behaviour must NOT change -- the driver reads upstream's "flow"
;  variable, not these bits.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPEJ.OUT> s16bdEJ.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 9600
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bdEJ.pkt
send rcvej.dat
statistics
